IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maca-core`

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- the questions of the person injured in a motor accident.
--
-- SEAT: the person injured in a motor accident: the "eligible person" while entitled, and "the claimant" once a claim is made.
-- "Am I covered? Am I excluded, or are my benefits reduced? What weekly amount do I get, and until when? What lump sum for my
-- impairment? Is this treatment covered? When must I claim, and when must I ask for a review?" Every question is phrased as that
-- person would ask it, on facts that person could state. Where the Act leaves a judgment to the Commission (that earning capacity is
-- reduced, an impairment's percentage, an emergency, a reasonable excuse), the question asks what the Commission decided, and the
-- answer is conditional on it. The rules are in maca-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates
-- no rule. The Commission and the designated person are the scheme's statutory decision makers: they get no seat.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY. Quotations of the Act and Regulations in maca-core.l4 are not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory (NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996; owner's ruling of 24 October 2026).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- the injured person's questions`

§§ `ss 4, 4A, 4B, 7 -- am I covered by the scheme`

@export Was I a resident of the Northern Territory at the time of my motor accident, for the motor accidents scheme (s 4B)?
GIVEN `I had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the accident, you had lived in the Northern Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months
      `I was not living in the Territory at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were not living in the Northern Territory
      `I had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been living outside the Northern Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more
      `my main home or main job was outside the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your primary dwelling house or your primary employment was outside the Northern Territory
      `I had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had left the Northern Territory intending no longer to live there
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I a Territory resident at my accident` IF
    `is a resident of the Territory` (`Residence` WITH
        `had resided in the Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months`        IS `I had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row`
        `was not living in the Territory at the time`                                      IS `I was not living in the Territory at the time`
        `had been living outside the Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more` IS `I had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more`
        `primary dwelling house or primary employment was not in the Territory`            IS `my main home or main job was outside the Territory`
        `had left the Territory intending no longer to reside there`                       IS `I had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere`)

@export Am I entitled to benefits under the Northern Territory motor accidents (no-fault) scheme for my injury (ss 4, 4A, 4B, 7)?
GIVEN `the vehicle was self-propelled, or a trailer attached to one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle involved was designed to be self-propelled (a car, motorbike, truck, bus and the like), or was a trailer attached to such a vehicle
      `the vehicle runs on rails` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was one that runs on rails, such as a train or tram
      `the vehicle is a slow motorised wheelchair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was a motorised wheelchair that cannot travel faster than 10 km/h
      `the vehicle is a cycle with an engine of 200 watts or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts
      `my injury came directly from the vehicle being driven` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle
      `my injury came directly from the vehicle moving out of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control
      `my injury came directly from a collision with the vehicle or from avoiding one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from a collision with the vehicle, moving or stationary, or from action to avoid a collision with it
      `I was hurt in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured in, or as a result of, the accident itself
      `I was hurt helping at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured while helping, or trying to help, at the scene of a motor accident
      `the accident happened in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in the Northern Territory
      `the accident happened in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in Australia (answer yes for an accident in the Territory)
      `a Territory-registered vehicle was in use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident was caused by, or arose out of, the use of a vehicle currently registered in the Northern Territory (including a federal interstate registration last made in the Territory)
      `I had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the accident, you had lived in the Northern Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months
      `I was not living in the Territory at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were not living in the Northern Territory
      `I had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been living outside the Northern Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more
      `my main home or main job was outside the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your primary dwelling house or your primary employment was outside the Northern Territory
      `I had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had left the Northern Territory intending no longer to live there
      `I have claimed damages where the accident happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident outside the Territory: whether you have made a claim for damages or compensation under the law of the State or Territory where it happened
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to motor accident benefits` IS
    `the s 7 entitlement for` `my occurrence` `at` `my place` `of a person with` `my residence` `who claimed elsewhere` `I have claimed damages where the accident happened`
    WHERE
        `my occurrence` MEANS
            `Occurrence` WITH
                `the vehicle` IS `Vehicle` WITH
                    `is designed to be self-propelled, or is a trailer attached to such a vehicle` IS `the vehicle was self-propelled, or a trailer attached to one`
                    `runs on rails`                                                               IS `the vehicle runs on rails`
                    `is a motorised wheelchair not capable of more than 10 km/h`                   IS `the vehicle is a slow motorised wheelchair`
                    `is a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts`                    IS `the vehicle is a cycle with an engine of 200 watts or less`
                `resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle`                                    IS `my injury came directly from the vehicle being driven`
                `resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control`                             IS `my injury came directly from the vehicle moving out of control`
                `resulted directly from a collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the vehicle` IS `my injury came directly from a collision with the vehicle or from avoiding one`
                `the person was killed or injured in it`                                               IS `I was hurt in the accident`
                `the person was killed or injured rendering assistance at the scene`                   IS `I was hurt helping at the scene`
        `my place` MEANS
            `Accident place` WITH
                `occurred in the Territory`                         IS `the accident happened in the Territory`
                `occurred in Australia`                             IS `the accident happened in Australia`
                `arose out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle` IS `a Territory-registered vehicle was in use`
        `my residence` MEANS
            `Residence` WITH
                `had resided in the Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months`        IS `I had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row`
                `was not living in the Territory at the time`                                      IS `I was not living in the Territory at the time`
                `had been living outside the Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more` IS `I had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more`
                `primary dwelling house or primary employment was not in the Territory`            IS `my main home or main job was outside the Territory`
                `had left the Territory intending no longer to reside there`                       IS `I had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere`

§§ `Part 3 -- am I excluded, or are my benefits reduced`

@export Must the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission presume that alcohol contributed to my accident (s 9(2); reg 4A)?
GIVEN `my highest breath alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest breath alcohol concentration from a breath analysis under the Traffic Act 1987, in grams per 210 litres of breath (for example 0.05); 0 if none
      `my highest blood alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest blood alcohol concentration from a blood sample taken within 4 hours of the accident, in grams per 100 millilitres (for example 0.05); 0 if none
      `I failed to give a breath or blood sample when required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were required under the Traffic Act 1987 to submit to a breath analysis or give a blood sample and did not
      `the Commission accepted I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for not giving the breath or blood sample
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` IF
    `the prescribed alcohol circumstances exist` (`Alcohol readings` WITH
        `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres`                                  IS `my highest breath alcohol reading`
        `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` IS `my highest blood alcohol reading`
        `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`                      IS `I failed to give a breath or blood sample when required`
        `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`                         IS `the Commission accepted I had a reasonable excuse`)

@export Which of my motor accident benefits are excluded because of how the accident happened (Part 3: ss 9-10C)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (Part 3 as encoded applies to accidents on or after 1 July 2014)
      `I was driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a motor vehicle when the accident happened
      `I was over the limit for alcohol or drugs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent that driving was (or on a public street would have been) a road traffic offence
      `my highest breath alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest breath alcohol concentration from a breath analysis under the Traffic Act 1987, in grams per 210 litres of breath; 0 if none
      `my highest blood alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest blood alcohol concentration from a blood sample taken within 4 hours of the accident, in grams per 100 millilitres; 0 if none
      `I failed to give a breath or blood sample when required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were required under the Traffic Act 1987 to submit to a breath analysis or give a blood sample and did not
      `the Commission accepted I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for not giving the breath or blood sample
      `the Commission considers the alcohol or drug contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident (asked where no presumption arises)
      `it has been shown the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident (this answers a presumption)
      `the Commission considers my conduct contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that your conduct contributed to the accident
      `I was found guilty for that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court found you guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or a dangerous driving offence
      `I recklessly ignored a substantial risk to myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were doing something that created a substantial risk of injury to yourself and recklessly ignored the risk (do not count not wearing a seatbelt or helmet)
      `I had never held a licence for that class of vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving and had never held a licence for that class of vehicle anywhere in Australia
      `my licence was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence was suspended at the time, other than to enforce a fine or penalty
      `my licence had been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence had been cancelled
      `my licence had expired 3 months or more before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident
      `I was driving in breach of my licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving in breach of the conditions of your licence
      `the Commission considers it was an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency
      `I was in a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in a motor vehicle when the accident happened
      `I owned that vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the owner of the vehicle you were in
      `it had been unregistered for 3 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle you were in was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months
      `it was a vehicle that could not be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle you were in was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B (for example a pre-1971 vehicle that cannot meet safety standards, or one never given a compliance plate)
      `I knew or should have known it was unregistered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as its driver, you knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered
      `it was conditionally registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle you were in was registered subject to conditions or restrictions
      `I knew or should have known it was conditionally registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as its driver, you knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered
      `it was driven in breach of its registration conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle you were in was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration
      `another registered vehicle being driven lawfully was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident involved another vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions
      `I stole or unlawfully used a vehicle involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a vehicle involved in the accident (whether or not convicted)
      `I was using a vehicle for an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were using a vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence
      `I was using a vehicle to escape or avoid arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were using a vehicle involved to escape from the scene of an offence, or to avoid apprehension or escape detention
      `I was using a vehicle intending to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were using a vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on yourself or another
      `my injury is covered by workers compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury is compensable under the Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) or another workers compensation law, or would be but for being self-inflicted or due to your serious and wilful misconduct
      `a vehicle in the accident was in a motor sport event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event (a race, competition, demonstration, trial or high speed test, organised or not, or preparations for one)
      `I was in that vehicle or involved in the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver of or a passenger in that vehicle, or an official or organiser, or assisting, or otherwise associated with the event
      `the accident was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act
GIVETH A `Part 3 exclusion`
DECIDE `Which of my benefits are excluded` IS
    `the Part 3 exclusion for` (`Part 3 facts` WITH
        `the day of the accident`                                                                       IS `the day of my accident`
        `was driving a motor vehicle`                                                                   IS `I was driving`
        `was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent of committing a road traffic offence` IS `I was over the limit for alcohol or drugs`
        `the alcohol readings` IS `Alcohol readings` WITH
            `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres`                                  IS `my highest breath alcohol reading`
            `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` IS `my highest blood alcohol reading`
            `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`                      IS `I failed to give a breath or blood sample when required`
            `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`                         IS `the Commission accepted I had a reasonable excuse`
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident`          IS `the Commission considers the alcohol or drug contributed`
        `it is established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident`                         IS `it has been shown the alcohol did not contribute`
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the person's conduct contributed to the accident`         IS `the Commission considers my conduct contributed`
        `has been found guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or dangerous driving` IS `I was found guilty for that conduct`
        `was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored the risk` IS `I recklessly ignored a substantial risk to myself`
        `had never held a licence for that class of motor vehicle`                                       IS `I had never held a licence for that class of vehicle`
        `the licence was suspended, other than to enforce a fine or penalty`                            IS `my licence was suspended`
        `the licence had been cancelled`                                                                IS `my licence had been cancelled`
        `the licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident`                       IS `my licence had expired 3 months or more before`
        `was driving in breach of the conditions of the licence`                                        IS `I was driving in breach of my licence conditions`
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`            IS `the Commission considers it was an emergency`
        `was in a motor vehicle`                                                                        IS `I was in a motor vehicle`
        `was the owner of that motor vehicle`                                                           IS `I owned that vehicle`
        `that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months`                              IS `it had been unregistered for 3 months or more`
        `that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B`                                               IS `it was a vehicle that could not be registered`
        `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered`                                 IS `I knew or should have known it was unregistered`
        `that vehicle was conditionally registered`                                                     IS `it was conditionally registered`
        `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered`                     IS `I knew or should have known it was conditionally registered`
        `that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration` IS `it was driven in breach of its registration conditions`
        `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions` IS `another registered vehicle being driven lawfully was involved`
        `was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a motor vehicle involved`          IS `I stole or unlawfully used a vehicle involved`
        `was using a motor vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence`           IS `I was using a vehicle for an indictable offence`
        `was using a motor vehicle involved to escape from an offence or to avoid apprehension or detention` IS `I was using a vehicle to escape or avoid arrest`
        `was using a motor vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another` IS `I was using a vehicle intending to cause death or injury`
        `the injury or death is compensable under workers compensation legislation, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct` IS `my injury is covered by workers compensation`
        `a motor vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event`                               IS `a vehicle in the accident was in a motor sport event`
        `was its driver or passenger, or an official or organiser of the event, or assisting or otherwise associated with it` IS `I was in that vehicle or involved in the event`
        `it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act`                              IS `the accident was a terrorist act`)

@export Are my weekly compensation and impairment lump sum reduced by 25% because I was not wearing a seatbelt or helmet (s 11)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (s 11 applies only to a person 16 or older at the accident)
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet that the Traffic Act 1987 (or the law where the accident happened) required, with no exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` IF
    `s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `my date of birth` `on` `the day of my accident`) `who` `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`

§§ `ss 13, 14 -- weekly compensation for loss of earning capacity`

@export On what day does my weekly compensation for loss of earning capacity stop: at pension age, or 104 weeks after the accident (s 13(5)(a))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `the day I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) s 23 (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957; the Social Security Act encoding answers it)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my weekly compensation stop` IS
    `the day the s 13 entitlement stops, for an accident on` `the day of my accident` `and pension age on` `the day I reach pension age`

@export If I was under 15, or a full-time student, at the accident, from what day can I be paid weekly compensation (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I was a full-time student at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a full-time student at a school, college or university at the accident, with no substantial break in your studies
      `I was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married, or in a relationship the Commission considers a de facto relationship, at the accident
      `my earnings were low in the 3 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your earnings from work in the 3 months before the accident were no more than 25% of what the Commission considers the average earnings of wage earners in the Territory for that period
      `I have stopped full-time study or married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since stopped being a full-time student, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship
      `the day I stopped full-time study or married` IS A DATE @desc The day you stopped being a full-time student, or married or entered a de facto relationship if that came sooner (any date if not yet)
GIVETH A `s 14(1) start`
DECIDE `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` IS
    `the s 14(1) start for` `me` `injured on` `the day of my accident`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS
            `Young person` WITH
                `the date of birth`                                                                              IS `my date of birth`
                `was a full-time student at the accident, with no substantial break in study`                     IS `I was a full-time student at the accident`
                `was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`                                       IS `I was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`
                `earned no more than 25% of average Territory wage earners' earnings in the 3 months before`      IS `my earnings were low in the 3 months before`
                `has since stopped full-time study, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship`         IS `I have stopped full-time study or married`
                `the day full-time study stopped, or of the marriage or de facto relationship if sooner`          IS `the day I stopped full-time study or married`
                -- Not read by s 14(1): a fixed placeholder.
                `by the week in question has married, entered a de facto relationship or had someone become primarily dependent on them` IS FALSE

@export If I am under 21, what percentage of the full weekly compensation do I get at my age (s 14(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the week you are asking about
      `I have married, entered a de facto relationship or have a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by that week, you have married, entered a relationship the Commission considers de facto, or had a child or other person become primarily dependent on you for financial support
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` IS
    `the s 14 percentage at age` (`the age of a person born` `my date of birth` `on` `the first day of the week`) `if` `I have married, entered a de facto relationship or have a dependant`

@export How much weekly compensation for loss of earning capacity do I get for this week, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 11, 11A, 13, 14)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (this encoding covers accidents on or after 31 May 2019)
      `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the week you are asking about (a week starting after the day of the accident)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) s 23 (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the Commission considers my earning capacity reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that your capacity to earn income from work, physical or mental, is reduced because of the injury
      `I was earning from work on the day of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were pension age or older at the accident: whether the Commission is satisfied that on that day you were someone who earned income from personal exertion
      `the maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum weekly amount (MA) the Commission has set for this half-year (from 1 January or 1 July): 85% of Territory average weekly earnings less notional income tax, in dollars
      `the Commission found I can work full time that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has determined you are capable of working full time that week, in any type of work
      `my earnings that week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earned from work that week, in dollars
      `the weekly amount the Commission calculated` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount the Commission calculated for you under s 13(3), from the hours it determined you can work, in dollars
      `I was in prison all that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were detained in a penal institution, in or outside the Territory, throughout that week
      `I was outside Australia all that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were outside Australia throughout that week
      `I was a full-time student at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a full-time student at a school, college or university at the accident, with no substantial break in your studies
      `I was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married, or in a relationship the Commission considers a de facto relationship, at the accident
      `my earnings were low in the 3 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your earnings from work in the 3 months before the accident were no more than 25% of what the Commission considers the average earnings of wage earners in the Territory for that period
      `I have stopped full-time study or married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since stopped being a full-time student, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship
      `the day I stopped full-time study or married` IS A DATE @desc The day you stopped being a full-time student, or married or entered a de facto relationship if that came sooner (any date if not yet)
      `I have married, entered a de facto relationship or have a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by that week, you have married, entered a relationship the Commission considers de facto, or had a child or other person become primarily dependent on you for financial support
      `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet that the Traffic Act 1987 (or the law where the accident happened) required, with no exemption
      `my other insurance set against the week` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) for the injury that the Commission sets against this week's payment, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A `Weekly benefit answer`
DECIDE `How much weekly compensation do I get this week` IS
    `the s 13 weekly benefit for` (`Earning capacity week` WITH
        `the day of the accident`                                                                         IS `the day of my accident`
        `the first day of the week`                                                                       IS `the first day of the week`
        `the day pension age is reached`                                                                  IS `the day I reach pension age`
        `the young person` IS `Young person` WITH
            `the date of birth`                                                                              IS `my date of birth`
            `was a full-time student at the accident, with no substantial break in study`                     IS `I was a full-time student at the accident`
            `was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`                                       IS `I was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`
            `earned no more than 25% of average Territory wage earners' earnings in the 3 months before`      IS `my earnings were low in the 3 months before`
            `has since stopped full-time study, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship`         IS `I have stopped full-time study or married`
            `the day full-time study stopped, or of the marriage or de facto relationship if sooner`          IS `the day I stopped full-time study or married`
            `by the week in question has married, entered a de facto relationship or had someone become primarily dependent on them` IS `I have married, entered a de facto relationship or have a dependant`
        `the Commission considers the capacity to earn from personal exertion reduced by the injury`      IS `the Commission considers my earning capacity reduced`
        `earned income from personal exertion on the day of the accident, as the Commission is satisfied` IS `I was earning from work on the day of the accident`
        `the maximum amount MA for the half-year`                                                         IS `the maximum weekly amount`
        `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week`                         IS `the Commission found I can work full time that week`
        `earnings from work that week`                                                                    IS `my earnings that week`
        `the weekly amount the Commission calculated under s 13(3)`                                        IS `the weekly amount the Commission calculated`
        `was detained in a penal institution throughout the week`                                          IS `I was in prison all that week`
        `was outside Australia throughout the week`                                                        IS `I was outside Australia all that week`
        `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required`                                 IS `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`
        `the s 11A entitlement set against the week`                                                       IS `my other insurance set against the week`)

§§ `s 17 -- lump sum for permanent impairment`

@export How much is my lump sum for permanent impairment, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 4C, 11, 11A, 17; reg 4)?
GIVEN `my assessed impairment percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of whole person permanent impairment the Commission assessed under the AMA Guides to the Evaluation of Permanent Impairment, 6th edition (for example 12)
      `Territory average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Territory average weekly earnings for the calendar year of payment: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for the Northern Territory last published before 1 January, in dollars
      `I will be in Australia when it is paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will be in Australia when the lump sum is paid
      `I have already been paid a lump sum for this impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been paid a lump sum based on an assessment of this impairment (even if it has since got worse)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet that the Traffic Act 1987 (or the law where the accident happened) required, with no exemption
      `my other insurance set against the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) for the injury that the Commission sets against this lump sum, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Impairment lump sum answer`
DECIDE `How much is my impairment lump sum` IS
    `the s 17 lump sum for` (`Impairment claim` WITH
        `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person`        IS `my assessed impairment percentage`
        `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`                         IS `Territory average weekly earnings`
        `is in Australia when the payment is made`                                 IS `I will be in Australia when it is paid`
        `a lump sum on an assessment of this impairment has already been paid`     IS `I have already been paid a lump sum for this impairment`
        `s 11 applies`                                                             IS `s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `my date of birth` `on` `the day of my accident`) `who` `I was not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`
        `the s 11A entitlement set against it`                                     IS `my other insurance set against the lump sum`)

§§ `s 18 -- medical and rehabilitation costs`

@export Is this medical or rehabilitation service covered by the motor accidents scheme (s 18; reg 4D)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (this encoding covers accidents on or after 1 July 2014)
      `it is treatment, care, rehabilitation, transport or hospital care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is medical, surgical or dental treatment; nursing or other professional care; training or education for rehabilitation; transport to and from treatment; or hospital or other institutional care
      `it is attendant care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is attendant care: personal care, or household services such as cooking, cleaning, laundry or gardening
      `it is provided outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is provided outside Australia
      `I need it because of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need the service as a result of your injury from the accident
      `the Commission accepts it is necessary and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission considers the service necessary and reasonable, having considered its benefit, appropriateness, alternatives, provider, cost effectiveness and duration (reg 4D)
GIVETH A `Medical answer`
DECIDE `Is this medical service covered` IS
    `the s 18 answer for` (`Medical service` WITH
        `the day of the accident`                                                     IS `the day of my accident`
        `is a medical and rehabilitation service listed in s 18(2)`                    IS `it is treatment, care, rehabilitation, transport or hospital care`
        `is an attendant care service (personal or household services)`               IS `it is attendant care`
        `is provided outside Australia`                                               IS `it is provided outside Australia`
        `is required as a result of the injury`                                       IS `I need it because of the injury`
        `the Commission considers it necessary and reasonable, having considered reg 4D` IS `the Commission accepts it is necessary and reasonable`)

§§ `ss 18BA-18BE -- attendant care` -- only if the injury left you needing personal or household care

@export Which attendant care benefits can I get, for an injury on or after 1 July 2014 (ss 18BB-18BE; regs 4E, 4F; Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (this encoding covers injuries on or after 1 July 2014)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your claim under the Act
      `the injury left me with an impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an impairment as a result of the injury
      `I need attendant care because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need attendant care services (personal care, or household services) because of the impairment
      `my injury is a Schedule 1 kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical specialist approved by the Commission certifies an injury of a kind in Schedule 1: spinal cord injury, brain injury, amputation, burns or blindness
      `the Schedule 1 criteria are met in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the specialist certifies that the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury are met in full
      `the Schedule 1 criteria are met apart from permanency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the specialist certifies that the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury are met, leaving aside any requirement that it be permanent
      `my injury is permanent and stable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is permanent and stable at the date of assessment
      `the Commission found exceptional circumstances for long-term care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that exceptional circumstances warrant long-term attendant care benefits
      `the Commission found exceptional circumstances for interim care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that exceptional circumstances warrant interim attendant care benefits
      `I have had interim care benefits for this impairment before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been eligible for interim attendant care benefits for the same impairment
      `the care meets s 18BE` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the care is provided in Australia, by an approved provider (or a person the Commission approves), and the Commission considers it necessary, reasonable, related to the injury and of an appropriate standard
GIVETH AN `Attendant care answer`
DECIDE `Which attendant care benefits can I get` IS
    `the attendant care eligibility for` (`Attendant care facts` WITH
        `the day of the accident`                                                                 IS `the day of my accident`
        `the date of birth`                                                                       IS `my date of birth`
        `the day the claim was made`                                                              IS `the day I made my claim`
        `suffers an impairment as a result of the injury`                                         IS `the injury left me with an impairment`
        `requires attendant care services in consequence of the impairment`                       IS `I need attendant care because of it`
        `has an injury of a kind listed in Schedule 1`                                            IS `my injury is a Schedule 1 kind`
        `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury in full`                                   IS `the Schedule 1 criteria are met in full`
        `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury, leaving aside any requirement of permanency` IS `the Schedule 1 criteria are met apart from permanency`
        `the injury is permanent and stable`                                                      IS `my injury is permanent and stable`
        `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant long-term benefits`           IS `the Commission found exceptional circumstances for long-term care`
        `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant interim benefits`             IS `the Commission found exceptional circumstances for interim care`
        `has already had interim benefits for the same impairment`                                IS `I have had interim care benefits for this impairment before`
        `the services meet s 18BE`                                                                IS `the care meets s 18BE`)

§§ `s 25, regs 5, 6 -- a lump sum instead of payments`

@export Can the Commission commute my weekly compensation to a single lump sum (s 25; reg 5)?
GIVEN `I am entitled to weekly compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation for loss of earning capacity
      `I have applied for a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Commission to commute your weekly compensation
      `the Commission considers my payments too small to be worth paying weekly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that the amount does not justify the administrative cost of periodic payments
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my weekly compensation be commuted` IF
    `the Commission may commute the weekly benefit under reg 5, for a person who` `I am entitled to weekly compensation` `and` `I have applied for a lump sum` `or where` `the Commission considers my payments too small to be worth paying weekly`

@export Can the Commission re-open a commutation of my weekly compensation (reg 5(5))?
GIVEN `it was made without my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commutation was made without your consent
      `my condition has got substantially worse since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your medical condition has substantially deteriorated since the date of the commutation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my commutation be re-opened` IF
    `the Commission may re-open a reg 5 commutation made` `it was made without my consent` `where` `my condition has got substantially worse since`

DECLARE `Overseas commutation answer` HAS
    `my weekly compensation can be commuted`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `my medical and rehabilitation compensation can be commuted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my long-term attendant care can be commuted`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the most the lump sum can be, in dollars`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the most of it that can be for medical and rehabilitation, in dollars` IS A NUMBER

@export If I live, or am moving to live, outside Australia, which of my benefits can be commuted to a lump sum, and up to how much (reg 6)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `I have applied for a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Commission to commute your benefits
      `I live outside Australia or am about to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ordinarily live outside Australia, or are about to leave Australia to live outside it for a substantial period
      `my assessed impairment percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of whole person permanent impairment the Commission assessed (reg 6 needs 15 or more)
      `my condition has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your medical condition has stabilised so that its future course can be predicted with reasonable certainty
      `I am entitled to weekly compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation for loss of earning capacity
      `I am entitled to medical and rehabilitation compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation for medical and rehabilitation services
      `I am entitled to long-term attendant care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to long-term attendant care benefits
      `the CPI for 1 July 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI (weighted average of the 8 capital cities, ABS) used for 1 July 2007
      `the CPI for 1 July in the financial year of my accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI used for 1 July in the financial year in which your accident happened
GIVETH AN `Overseas commutation answer`
DECIDE `What can be commuted if I move overseas` IS
    `Overseas commutation answer` WITH
        `my weekly compensation can be commuted`                     IS `the Commission may commute under reg 6, on` `my facts` `compensation for loss of earning capacity (s 13)` `if entitled` `I am entitled to weekly compensation`
        `my medical and rehabilitation compensation can be commuted` IS `the Commission may commute under reg 6, on` `my facts` `medical and rehabilitation compensation (s 18)` `if entitled` `I am entitled to medical and rehabilitation compensation`
        `my long-term attendant care can be commuted`                IS `the Commission may commute under reg 6, on` `my facts` `long-term attendant care benefits` `if entitled` `I am entitled to long-term attendant care`
        `the most the lump sum can be, in dollars`                   IS `the reg 3 indexed amount of` `the reg 6(4) total cap before indexation` `from CPI` `the CPI for 1 July 2007` `to CPI` `the CPI for 1 July in the financial year of my accident`
        `the most of it that can be for medical and rehabilitation, in dollars` IS `the reg 3 indexed amount of` `the reg 6(4) medical cap before indexation` `from CPI` `the CPI for 1 July 2007` `to CPI` `the CPI for 1 July in the financial year of my accident`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS
            `Reg 6 facts` WITH
                `the day of the accident`                                             IS `the day of my accident`
                `has applied`                                                         IS `I have applied for a lump sum`
                `is ordinarily resident outside Australia, or about to leave to live outside it for a substantial period` IS `I live outside Australia or am about to`
                `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person` IS `my assessed impairment percentage`
                `the medical condition has stabilised so its future course can be predicted with reasonable certainty` IS `my condition has stabilised`

§§ `s 7(3) -- claiming damages in another State or Territory` -- only for a Territory resident hurt elsewhere in Australia

@export If I claim damages where the accident happened, how much of the benefits already paid must I repay the Commission from what I am awarded (s 7(3)(c))?
GIVEN `benefits I have been paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory benefits already paid to you, or for your benefit, under the Act, in dollars
      `damages I am awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages or compensation awarded on your claim in the other State or Territory, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I repay from damages awarded elsewhere` IS
    `the s 7(3)(c)(ii) reimbursement of` `benefits I have been paid` `from` `damages I am awarded`

§§ `ss 31, 31A -- making my claim`

@export What is the last day I can claim before the Commission must refuse my claim as too late (s 31(3))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (for a claim to vary a benefit, the date of the change in circumstances)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (a claimant under 18 at the accident has until 3 years after turning 18)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can claim` IS
    `the last day for a claim the Commission must not refuse, for an accident on` `the day of my accident` `and a claimant born` `my date of birth`

@export What is the last day I can claim without the Commission being able to refuse it as late (s 31(2))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (for a claim to vary a benefit, the date of the change in circumstances)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can claim without risk of refusal` IS
    `the last day before the Commission may refuse a claim, for an accident on` `the day of my accident`

@export If I make my claim on this day, may or must the Commission refuse to consider it as late (s 31(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) your claim, in the approved form
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (for a claim to vary a benefit, the date of the change in circumstances)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A `Claim timing answer`
DECIDE `Is my claim in time` IS
    `the s 31 timing of a claim made on` `the day I make my claim` `for an accident on` `the day of my accident` `by a claimant born` `my date of birth`

@export May the Commission refuse my claim because, as the driver, I did not report the accident (s 31A)?
GIVEN `I was the driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver of a motor vehicle in the accident
      `I reported the accident as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reported the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 (NT) requires
      `the Commission accepts I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion you had a reasonable excuse for not reporting it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my claim be refused for not reporting the accident` IF
    `the Commission may refuse the claim under s 31A of a claimant who` `I was the driver` `and` `I reported the accident as required` `with excuse` `the Commission accepts I had a reasonable excuse`

§§ `Part 6 -- review and the Tribunal` -- only if the Commission has decided your claim and you disagree

@export What is the last day I can ask the designated person to review a decision on my claim (s 28A(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice of the decision on your claim (or, with no notice, the day you became aware of it)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to ask for a review` IS
    `the day` `the days to ask for a review` `days after` `the day I received notice of the decision`

@export By what day must the designated person decide my review (s 28B(1)(c), (3))?
GIVEN `the day I asked for the review` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your request for review, in the approved form
      `public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Northern Territory public holidays fall on a weekday in the 30 business days after your request (each adds a business day); 0 if none
      `I was asked to a conference or for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the designated person gave you written notice asking you to attend a conference or give more information
      `days from that notice until I attended or gave it` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from that notice to the conference or to your giving the information
      `days that notice allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from that notice to the time it stated for the conference or the information
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my review be decided` IS
    `the last day for the review decision on a request made` `the day I asked for the review` `with` `public holidays on weekdays in the period` `holidays, a conference or information requested` `I was asked to a conference or for more information` `taking` `days from that notice until I attended or gave it` `of` `days that notice allowed`

@export What is the last day I can refer my claim to the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Appeal Tribunal (s 28E(3))?
GIVEN `a review decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the designated person has made a decision on your review
      `the day I received notice of the review decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice of the review decision (or, with no notice, the day you became aware of it); any date if none was made
      `the day I asked for the review` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your request for review
      `public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Northern Territory public holidays fall on a weekday in the 30 business days after your request; 0 if none
      `I was asked to a conference or for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the designated person gave you written notice asking you to attend a conference or give more information
      `days from that notice until I attended or gave it` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from that notice to the conference or to your giving the information
      `days that notice allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from that notice to the time it stated for the conference or the information
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to go to the Tribunal` IS
    IF `a review decision has been made`
    THEN `the day` `the days to refer to the Tribunal` `days after` `the day I received notice of the review decision`
    ELSE `the day` `the days to refer to the Tribunal` `days after` (`the last day for the review decision on a request made` `the day I asked for the review` `with` `public holidays on weekdays in the period` `holidays, a conference or information requested` `I was asked to a conference or for more information` `taking` `days from that notice until I attended or gave it` `of` `days that notice allowed`)
